# Docker Task — Fix Dockerfile Build on App Server 1

## 📌 Project Overview

This task involved troubleshooting and fixing a Dockerfile for Nautilus DevOps in the Stratos Datacenter (Stratos DC).

The Dockerfile was located in `/opt/docker` on **App Server 1 (`stapp01`)**. The initial Docker build failed because the Dockerfile was not being read from the correct directory and attempts to overwrite it encountered permission issues.

The Dockerfile was corrected, and the image was built successfully using the existing Apache HTTP Server base image.

## 🎯 Task Objectives

- Troubleshoot the Docker build failure.
- Fix the Dockerfile while preserving valid configuration.
- Keep the original base image, `httpd:2.4.43`.
- Configure Apache to listen on port `8080`.
- Enable the required SSL modules and SSL configuration.
- Copy the existing SSL certificate, private key, and HTML page into the image.
- Build the Docker image successfully.

