## 🔐 Important Notes

- The original base image, `httpd:2.4.43`, was preserved.
- The existing application HTML file was not replaced with new content.
- The required SSL files were copied from the existing build context.
- The Dockerfile was written using elevated permissions.
- The image was built from the correct directory.
- A successful image build does not by itself prove that Apache starts correctly or that HTTPS connections work; those would require separate runtime tests.

